## The 5 findings that matter most (read George's attention here)

1. **ЮЗУ already runs StrikePlagiarism inside Blackboard.** Verified from the official ЮЗУ disted.swu.bg student manual — homework submitted via Blackboard Assignments goes through it, students see the similarity report, resubmissions are professor-controlled. This is the system George will actually face.

2. **ЮЗУ requires a signed authorship declaration** for every курсова работа/реферат (official PDF on stf.swu.bg) — and it grants ЮЗУ the right to **archive the paper permanently**. Two "independent" versions must therefore also not trip next year's checks.

3. **Turnitin's AI detector has no Bulgarian model** (official release notes: English, Spanish, Japanese only — verified). Bulgarian referats are effectively invisible to AI detection; only text-matching applies. But since Aug 2025 Turnitin **detects humanizer/bypasser tools themselves** on English text — so commercial "humanizers" are now a liability, not a shield.

4. **Tome is dead** (tome.app returns DEPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND; pivoted to sales AI in 2024). **Gamma is the only strong SaaS**: PPTX export confirmed, real API GA since Nov 2025 (Pro+ required). But the default should be **python-pptx (v1.0.2) + LLM** — it's the only path that follows a professor's strict template exactly in Bulgarian.

5. **Telegram ingestion is free and simple**: BotFather token + `getUpdates` long polling (no server), 20 MB file download / 50 MB upload — far above any referat size. Valeria just needs to /start the bot once.

Honest gaps, marked **[UNVERIFIED]** in the report: Gamma's exact dollar prices (pricing page is JS-rendered, Internet Archive was offline), exact similarity thresholds (no BG university publishes one — UNWE's procedure confirms scope but not a %), and referat page-count norms (BG-wide custom 8–15 pages, no official ЮЗУ doc found).
